---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import ConfirmOfficial from "../components/ConfirmOfficial.astro";
---

<Base
  title="Company and active residency"
  description="Forming an Andorran SL and applying for self-employed residency: capital, 34%, AFA, 183 days, CASS."
  path="/company-active-residency"
>
  <section class="page-header">
    <h1>Company and active residency</h1>
    <p>
      If you will work here, this is the ordinary private route. The
      company is not a mailbox. The days are not optional.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="prose">
    <p class="as-of">As of 29 August 2026</p>
    <ConfirmOfficial />

    <p>
      As of 29 August 2026, the standard entrepreneur path is:
      incorporate an Andorran limited company (usually an SL), hold a
      real controlling stake — commonly more than 34% — occupy a
      management role, pay the AFA contribution now treated as
      non-refundable for new files, live here 183 days a year, and join
      CASS. Foreign-investment authorisation is required when a
      non-resident takes a qualifying stake.
    </p>
    <p>
      The Government’s J.1 page is
      <a
        href="https://www.govern.ad/ca/tematiques/immigracio/residencia-i-treball/residencia-i-treball-per-compte-propi-autoritzacio-inicial"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener"
        >residència i treball per compte propi</a
      >.
      Decret 75/2026 set a general self-employed quota of 200
      authorisations: 150 for foreign-investment cases, 50 for liberal
      professions. Check whether a place is actually being issued.
    </p>

    <h2>The company</h2>
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>Form</th>
          <th>Minimum capital</th>
          <th>Usual use</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td>SL / SLU</td>
          <td>€3,000 paid up</td>
          <td>
            Services, consultancies, ordinary trading, most new arrivals.
          </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>SA</td>
          <td>€60,000</td>
          <td>Larger or more formal. Rarely the first company.</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p>
      Those capital figures are on the Government’s
      <a
        href="https://www.govern.ad/ca/tematiques/empresa-i-emprenedoria/creacio-i-modificacio-d-empreses/punt-empresa/fase-de-constitucio-de-la-societat"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener">constitution page</a
      >.
      Headline corporate tax is 10%, as stated on the official
      <a
        href="https://www.e-tramits.ad/tramits/impostos/is"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener">Impost sobre Societats</a
      >
      note. IGI is 4.5%. Andorra will not defend a shell. A company with
      no office, no real management here and no activity is a problem
      for the bank, for CASS and for Immigration. Substance is the
      point.
    </p>

    <h2>How incorporation usually runs</h2>
    <p>
      NIA; reserved company name (CCIS / denominació social); foreign-
      investment authorisation if you are a non-resident; an Andorran
      bank account to hold the capital; statutes, usually in Catalan; a
      public deed before a notary; inscription; NRT; CASS if you will
      employ or if the residency file requires it; a parish trade
      licence if you will open a comerç. A clean file is often four to
      eight weeks. The bank and foreign-investment can double that.
      Budget several thousand euros in professional and notary costs on
      top of the €3,000 capital — not including the AFA payment attached
      to the residency. We do not invent gestoria fees beyond that
      budget.
    </p>
    <p>
      The companion Government page is
      <a
        href="https://www.govern.ad/ca/tematiques/empresa-i-emprenedoria/creacio-i-modificacio-d-empreses/punt-empresa/creacio-d-una-empresa-a-andorra"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener">Creació d’una empresa a Andorra</a
      >.
    </p>

    <h2>The residency attached</h2>
    <p>
      Stake commonly more than 34% and effective management. AFA
      €50,000 for new self-employed files under Llei 2/2026; treat as
      non-refundable if granted. 183 days. CASS employer/employee
      commonly cited about 15.5% and 6.5%, self-employed around 22% of
      the chosen base — use current
      <a href="https://www.cass.ad/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">CASS</a>
      tables, not this sentence, for the payment.
    </p>

    <h2>What usually breaks it</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>A mailbox company with no management here.</li>
      <li>A stake that is not a real controlling position.</li>
      <li>Treating 183 days as optional.</li>
      <li>Not joining CASS when the file requires it.</li>
      <li>A bank that will not take the capital or the source of wealth.</li>
      <li>
        Paying the AFA sum as if it were still a refundable deposit.
      </li>
      <li>Starting after the J.1 quota for the year has closed.</li>
    </ul>

    <p>
      Related:
      <a href="/residency-vs-tax">Three things people confuse</a>,
      <a href="/the-file">The file and the bank</a>.
    </p>
  </section>
</Base>
